{
  "_doc": [
    "Kanji/kana menu graphics redrawn in English by tools/menus.py.",
    "tileset: ROM offset of the 4 KB tile block the screen loads; a tile's data is at tileset + (VRAM address & 0xFFF).",
    "signed: true if the screen uses 8800 addressing (LCDC bit 4 = 0), so tile t is at 0x9000 + signed(t)*16.",
    "cells: tilemap rows (screen row -> {first column, tile numbers}); only these tiles get rewritten.",
    "  Cells using the shared blank tile 00 are not listed, so ink there is an error.",
    "clear: screen pixel rectangle [x0, y0, x1, y1] (inclusive) blanked before drawing.",
    "lines: text drawn in the font/menu5x7.txt font; y is the top pixel; x is the left pixel or \"center\" around cx.",
    "Positions come from PyBoy captures of the original screens.",
    "ink/paper: colors for text and the cleared box (default 3 on 0). Course names are white (0) on black (3)."
